From: Chaz Bailey <charles.s.bailey@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: mux: wcd939x: keep USB 2.0 enabled in DP AltMode Pin Assignment C and E

Under the USB Type-C Cable and Connector Specification, the USB 2.0 differential
pair (D+ and D-) is completely independent of the SuperSpeed multiplexing.
Even in DisplayPort AltMode Pin Assignment C and E (where all 4 high-speed lanes
are allocated to DisplayPort), USB 2.0 remains fully active and operational.

The WCD9395 USBSS mux only switches D+/D- and SBU1/SBU2 (as well as analog
audio lines for AATC accessory mode). When entering TYPEC_DP_STATE_C or
TYPEC_DP_STATE_E, the driver previously cleared enable_usb and only set
enable_dp, physically disconnecting the D+ and D- lines from the SoC's eUSB2
repeater/PHY. This prevented USB 2.0 peripherals (such as USB audio and IMU
sensors built into AR glasses like Nreal Air, or USB 2.0 hubs on USB-C monitors)
from enumerating when 4-lane DisplayPort was active.

Keep enable_usb = true in TYPEC_DP_STATE_C and TYPEC_DP_STATE_E so that USB 2.0
remains routed and functional alongside 4-lane DisplayPort Alt Mode.

--- a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c
@@ -256,6 +256,7 @@ static int wcd939x_usbss_set(struct wcd939x_usbss *usbss)
 		/* DP Only */
 		case TYPEC_DP_STATE_C:
 		case TYPEC_DP_STATE_E:
+			enable_usb = true;
 			enable_dp = true;
 			break;
 
